# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is never committed.
# Every variable is validated with zod at startup, so a missing required value
# crashes the process immediately instead of failing at first use.
#
# HOW MUCH OF THIS YOU ACTUALLY NEED depends on how you start the app:
#
#   shopify app dev            DATABASE_URL only.
#                              The CLI runs the app itself and injects
#                              SHOPIFY_API_KEY, SHOPIFY_API_SECRET, HOST (the
#                              tunnel URL), SCOPES and PORT. HOST and SCOPES are
#                              read under those names — see
#                              apps/admin-app/src/server/cli-env-aliases.ts.
#
#   pnpm --filter admin-app dev
#                              Everything below. You are then responsible for
#                              the tunnel and for keeping the app URL and
#                              callback URL in the dashboard in step with it.
#
# Either way the app is embedded: it only opens from inside a store's admin.
# Visiting the server directly answers 400 "No shop provided", which is the
# install check working, not a fault. See docs/development.md.

# --- Shopify app ---
# From the app in your dashboard. `shopify app config link` writes the client id
# into shopify.app.toml; the secret is only ever in .env.
SHOPIFY_API_KEY=
SHOPIFY_API_SECRET=
# Must be HTTPS. The admin is HTTPS and frames the app in an iframe, so an http
# app URL is blocked as mixed content by the browser before we see it.
SHOPIFY_APP_URL=https://your-tunnel.example.com
# Must stay identical to [access_scopes] in shopify.app.toml — that is what the
# merchant actually granted, and a disagreement puts the app in a scope-update
# loop on every load.
#
# read/write_metaobject_definitions are required by the install step: the app
# creates the `ingredient` metaobject definition and the custom.* metafield
# definitions itself (ADR-0003). Confirmed against the 2026-07 schema through
# the Shopify Dev MCP, which reports the scopes each operation needs.
SHOPIFY_SCOPES=read_products,write_products,read_inventory,write_inventory,read_orders,read_metaobject_definitions,write_metaobject_definitions
SHOPIFY_STORE=your-store.myshopify.com

# The Admin API version is deliberately NOT here. It is a code-level
# compatibility contract tied to the queries in this repository, so it lives in
# packages/shared/src/api-version.ts and is not overridable per environment.

# --- Database ---
# Local PostgreSQL. If you don't have one: docker compose up -d
# Rationale for the database and ORM choice: docs/adr/0007-database-and-orm.md
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://nordlys:nordlys@localhost:5432/nordlys?schema=public

# --- Mock ERP (roadmap v2) ---
ERP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
ERP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Misc ---
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=debug
